title: "A Jet-Multiplicity Confound in Reconstruction-Based Anomaly Detection: Evidence from a Higgs-to-Tau-Pair Proxy Signal"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Arun"
    given-names: "Abhijay"
version: "v2-revision"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23325916"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abhijay-MSD/higgs-anomaly-detection"
abstract: "Code and results for testing whether PCA, autoencoder and variational autoencoder reconstruction error, trained on simulated background events only, can flag an unseen proxy signal in the ATLAS Higgs Boson Machine Learning Challenge 2014 dataset, with a jet-count control, baselines, latent-code scores, retraining without jet inputs, synthetic and energy-scale shifts, and latent-space analysis."
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - autoencoder
  - high-energy physics
  - representation learning